questions.solution_explanation:
In a **disconnected graph**, a single BFS/DFS from one vertex can only visit all vertices reachable from that starting vertex — other connected components remain unvisited. The standard solution:
```
for (int v = 0; v < V; v++)
    if (!visited[v])
        BFS_or_DFS(v);
```
Each call to BFS/DFS explores one connected component. The total number of such calls equals the number of connected components. Adding a virtual super-source (option C) works but is a different technique used in network flow algorithms.
